00:48:20.170 --> 00:48:21.850
Yes, and I'll tell everyone,

00:48:21.870 --> 00:48:23.610
but the only way I can is if I win.

00:48:23.810 --> 00:48:25.710
And to win, you need to get across the room.

00:48:26.750 --> 00:48:27.190
Exactly.

00:48:27.970 --> 00:48:29.960
Well, I hate the idea of...

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:31.440
of you winning any race.

00:48:32.000 --> 00:48:34.540
But it's more important for Ramford to be humiliated.

00:48:34.830 --> 00:48:35.590
Back us up.

00:48:45.110 --> 00:48:54.880
We're gonna remain close.

00:48:55.040 --> 00:48:55.640
Thanks for the help.

00:48:55.720 --> 00:48:56.600
You fool.

00:48:56.940 --> 00:48:58.360
What, you're still mad?

00:48:58.540 --> 00:48:59.840
Yes, you're wasting time.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:01.800
Go beat Ranford.

00:49:01.960 --> 00:49:02.620
Oh, right.

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:04.240
Seriously, thanks.

00:49:07.990 --> 00:49:09.770
Annalise had to get her goodness from somewhere.

00:49:25.100 --> 00:49:27.020
Lucy, Chim-Chim, it's time for that picture.

00:49:31.400 --> 00:49:35.580
A photo of him pouring those cans into the fuel tank proves the soda is actually gasoline.

00:49:35.800 --> 00:49:37.580
Oh, don't remind me.

00:49:37.920 --> 00:49:43.130
I'm sorry, there's something wrong with the zoom. I can't get a closer shot.

00:49:43.370 --> 00:49:44.630
We'll just have to get closer.

00:49:46.250 --> 00:49:49.520
Everything's going as planned. I'm a shoo-in to win now.

00:49:49.680 --> 00:49:52.520
But none of it would be possible without you, my sweet.

00:49:53.260 --> 00:49:54.760
Lucy, can you get a clear shot?

00:49:54.920 --> 00:49:56.780
I can, if Connor gets out of my way.

00:49:57.380 --> 00:49:57.960
All clear.

00:49:58.720 --> 00:49:59.200
I got...

00:50:02.680 --> 00:50:04.580
Who's over there?

00:50:05.130 --> 00:50:06.150
He's headed this way.

00:50:06.350 --> 00:50:06.570
Okay.

00:50:06.870 --> 00:50:08.250
On the count of three, we break through.

00:50:08.870 --> 00:50:10.010
One, two...

00:50:10.520 --> 00:50:10.820
One!

00:50:11.380 --> 00:50:12.220
You with the camera!

00:50:12.700 --> 00:50:13.720
You stop right there!

00:50:14.950 --> 00:50:16.230
Lucy, hold on to that camera!

00:50:16.390 --> 00:50:17.490
It's the evidence we need!

00:50:17.630 --> 00:50:19.750
I'm worried about him getting us, not the camera!

00:50:20.760 --> 00:50:22.220
Lex, don't fail me now!

00:51:59.370 --> 00:51:59.670
children.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:01.780
I can't let you leave with that camera.

00:52:02.020 --> 00:52:03.260
People need to know the truth.

00:52:03.540 --> 00:52:05.680
The truth is a luxury I can't afford.

00:52:06.110 --> 00:52:10.410
Give me that camera, or my friend here will blow up your precious Mach 6.

00:52:10.710 --> 00:52:11.830
We can't give it to him.

00:52:11.950 --> 00:52:13.510
The camera's got the proof we need.

00:52:13.630 --> 00:52:15.030
And Chim Chim is still in there.

00:52:15.250 --> 00:52:17.880
But if he blows up the Mach 6, we'll lose everything.

00:52:18.160 --> 00:52:18.840
What should we do?

00:52:19.970 --> 00:52:23.340
The other racers.

00:52:24.080 --> 00:52:25.880
Your Naptics cost me my lead.

00:52:26.100 --> 00:52:27.360
I was miles ahead.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:36.170
Good little way, sir.

00:52:41.880 --> 00:52:42.520
...down eventually.

00:52:42.740 --> 00:52:44.440
No, I really won't.

00:52:46.020 --> 00:52:46.540
What the?

00:52:47.270 --> 00:52:49.530
You thought you could steal gas from me?

00:52:49.630 --> 00:52:52.270
I just wanted to be a great eco-hero like you.

00:52:52.410 --> 00:52:53.250
Watch your tongue.

00:52:53.490 --> 00:52:54.250
Why did you do it?

00:52:54.790 --> 00:52:56.790
Why did you lie about the eco-car?

00:52:57.380 --> 00:52:58.900
That engine was our dream.

00:52:59.660 --> 00:52:59.980
You're not...

00:53:00.220 --> 00:53:06.120
but a phony no claiming to have an eco car is just as good as having one look at all the free

00:53:06.120 --> 00:53:11.600
publicity it's already gotten me but it doesn't exist only you and your friends know that and now

00:53:11.600 --> 00:53:23.060
that i have your camera no one will ever believe you you never learn there's no stopping us now

00:53:34.120 --> 00:53:36.540
I'm sorry, Speed. We tried, and we failed.

00:53:36.720 --> 00:53:38.840
Nothing can stop Ranford from winning the race now.

00:53:42.100 --> 00:53:44.720
This is so horrible! Ranford's going to win the race!

00:53:44.760 --> 00:53:47.820
He's so far ahead of everybody else. Nothing can stop him now.

00:53:47.900 --> 00:53:49.040
Don't be so sure.

00:53:49.240 --> 00:53:49.780
What do you mean?

00:53:49.900 --> 00:53:51.320
Do you know something we don't?

00:53:51.480 --> 00:53:54.320
Remember how Ranford caught me with a cola can filled with gas?

00:53:54.540 --> 00:53:56.000
It got Port and Swiss fuel tank.

00:53:56.140 --> 00:53:59.740
It wasn't one of his gas cans. It was a real can filled with Ranford cola.

00:54:00.440 --> 00:54:02.920
The sugar in that soda will wreck the engine!

00:54:03.310 --> 00:54:06.330
Exactly. And it should be happening any moment now.

00:54:07.800 --> 00:54:23.140
The moment we've been waiting for,

00:54:23.540 --> 00:54:25.440
a few hundred yards away from the finish line,

00:54:25.560 --> 00:54:28.640
is Nicky Radford's Every Day is Earth Day echo car.

00:54:31.790 --> 00:54:35.170
Wait a second, it appears Frankfurt is having some sort of mechanical difficulty.

00:54:40.700 --> 00:54:44.340
And it looks like there's some sort of black cloud coming out of his car.

00:54:44.660 --> 00:54:45.900
But how can that be?

00:54:46.200 --> 00:54:48.590
It worked! There's no way he can win now.

00:54:48.810 --> 00:54:50.810
Well, at least we know someone else will get to run his company.

00:54:51.070 --> 00:54:52.140
I just wish it was us.

00:54:52.340 --> 00:54:53.300
Why do you think it won't be?

00:54:53.440 --> 00:54:54.780
We're completely out of fuel.

00:54:56.860 --> 00:54:58.600
Heard the wind's blowing up a gale today.

00:54:58.920 --> 00:54:59.780
Avast, mateys!

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.640
The HMS Mach 6 shall sail again!

00:55:02.840 --> 00:55:03.400
All right!

00:55:04.040 --> 00:55:14.210
Leave it, folks.

00:55:14.660 --> 00:55:15.720
I thought I'd seen everything,

00:55:15.900 --> 00:55:18.540
but it looks like Ranford's trying to win this race with elbow grease.

00:55:19.450 --> 00:55:20.110
What's that?

00:55:21.970 --> 00:55:23.050
Get what I just said.

00:55:23.380 --> 00:55:24.500
Now I've seen everything.

00:55:24.760 --> 00:55:26.120
Here comes the Mach 6.

00:55:26.320 --> 00:55:27.780
It's doing about six knots.

00:55:28.960 --> 00:55:29.980
Get ready for...

00:55:34.480 --> 00:55:39.130
Kicked him!

00:56:01.360 --> 00:56:05.440
Now you're about to caught a robot monkey this big?

00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:13.430
You think it's time we go into business together?

00:56:13.670 --> 00:56:13.990
Yeah!

00:56:16.200 --> 00:56:16.720
Leave it!

00:56:17.140 --> 00:56:17.960
The Mach 6 run!

00:56:18.220 --> 00:56:19.540
The Mach 6 run!

00:56:22.130 --> 00:56:22.470
Get it!

00:56:30.860 --> 00:56:38.750
This is the marvelous team up of X and Annalise.

00:56:38.850 --> 00:56:39.890
They're followed by...

00:56:39.890 --> 00:56:41.630
Oh, well, everyone else.

00:56:42.730 --> 00:56:47.740
Some good news and some bad news.

00:56:47.940 --> 00:56:48.860
What's the good news?

00:56:49.180 --> 00:56:50.480
We didn't come in third.

00:56:50.760 --> 00:56:51.760
And the bad news?

00:56:52.090 --> 00:56:53.590
We came in last.

00:56:54.510 --> 00:56:55.070
Hmm.

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:02.430
You look happy, Mr. Zazek.

00:57:02.600 --> 00:57:07.400
Well, I'm not happy I lost, but I am happy if Ranford lost, so thank you for that.

00:57:08.610 --> 00:57:11.550
That's got to be the weirdest thank you I've ever heard.

00:57:11.770 --> 00:57:15.200
Great work, bro. You beat a trillionaire and a billionaire.

00:57:15.700 --> 00:57:18.540
Um, no offense about that billionaire being your father.

00:57:18.740 --> 00:57:20.580
You just had to bring that up, didn't you?

00:57:21.030 --> 00:57:24.130
You're only a billionaire? You know what that means?

00:57:24.530 --> 00:57:27.190
Since Speed won the race, he's got more money than you.

00:57:27.350 --> 00:57:28.450
You need a loan, Annalise?

00:57:28.490 --> 00:57:29.970
Ew, gross. I wouldn't touch...

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:32.120
your nerd money with a 10-foot pole.

00:57:33.820 --> 00:57:36.860
Being a trillionaire means never having to say you're sorry.

00:57:37.300 --> 00:57:39.540
Text message my helicopter to pick us up.

00:57:42.230 --> 00:57:43.170
Drop the phone.

00:57:47.850 --> 00:57:50.570
The security will be holding you until the proper authorities arrive.

00:57:50.850 --> 00:57:51.570
It doesn't matter.

00:57:52.030 --> 00:57:54.350
I'm rich enough to buy my way out of jail.

00:57:54.510 --> 00:57:56.470
Not if I confess our crimes.

00:57:56.670 --> 00:57:58.470
I've never heard you talk before.

00:57:58.810 --> 00:57:59.970
That's because I just don't...

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:26.840
like you it's time we reintroduce ourselves to an old friend make sure you get one of lucy

00:58:26.900 --> 00:58:29.700
our ace photographer never gets to be in any of her own photos

00:58:36.280 --> 00:58:41.040
speed speed yes there have been reports of black smoke coming out of ranford's eco car

00:58:41.040 --> 00:58:47.430
would you like to comment dickie ranford's eco car was a sham as you can see here his car had an

00:58:47.430 --> 00:58:52.840
emissions collector it hit the fact that his car was running on leaded gasoline but where was he

00:58:52.840 --> 00:58:57.380
getting this gasoline he never refueled at the checkpoints he hid it in cans of ranford cola

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:02.750
I can't believe it. There never was an eco-car?

00:59:02.930 --> 00:59:04.090
No, it was a lie.

00:59:04.290 --> 00:59:07.180
But now that I'm head of Ranford Automotive, I make one.

00:59:07.380 --> 00:59:09.060
Let's put oil companies out of business

00:59:09.060 --> 00:59:11.260
and drive cars that really are eco-friendly.

00:59:12.500 --> 00:59:14.600
You really think your company's up for the challenge?

00:59:14.740 --> 00:59:16.860
It will be, once I hire my new designer

00:59:16.860 --> 00:59:19.080
and my new administrator.

00:59:20.170 --> 00:59:21.850
My team will make something better

00:59:21.850 --> 00:59:23.630
than the fake car Ranford promised.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:33.100
The second time today, you've turned your frown upside down.

00:59:33.280 --> 00:59:33.580
What?

00:59:33.820 --> 00:59:34.720
You're smiling.

00:59:35.060 --> 00:59:36.580
I suppose I am.

00:59:37.050 --> 00:59:37.630
But why?

00:59:37.950 --> 00:59:39.930
Speed took over your rival company

00:59:39.930 --> 00:59:43.590
and promised to put oil out of business by making eco-cars.

00:59:43.810 --> 00:59:45.250
Thanks for reminding me.

00:59:45.510 --> 00:59:46.130
It's all right.

00:59:46.290 --> 00:59:47.270
I am happy.

00:59:47.610 --> 00:59:49.710
Speed exposed Ranford, which is good for me.

00:59:49.910 --> 00:59:52.930
And he took over his company, which is great for me.

00:59:53.370 --> 00:59:53.710
What?

00:59:54.070 --> 00:59:56.290
That kid still has a lot to learn about business.

00:59:56.290 --> 00:59:59.090
He's no threat to me or my oil empire.

01:00:27.490 --> 01:00:28.890
Hmm.

01:00:30.720 --> 01:00:31.140
Thanks!

01:00:31.700 --> 01:00:33.540
I've never been prouder of you kids.

01:00:33.880 --> 01:00:36.860
That was an incredibly intense race, and you made it on your own.

01:00:36.960 --> 01:00:37.320
Thanks!

01:00:37.680 --> 01:00:38.720
Actually, I'm glad you're here.

01:00:38.980 --> 01:00:41.360
I was hoping you knew when we'd get to take over Ranford Automotive.

01:00:41.380 --> 01:00:41.500
Speed!

01:00:43.120 --> 01:00:44.000
Tell us, Speed!

01:00:44.240 --> 01:00:45.560
How do you feel about the big news?

01:00:45.740 --> 01:00:46.320
What big news?

01:00:46.500 --> 01:00:49.940
The stockholders of Ranford Automotive were very unhappy over his lies.

01:00:50.180 --> 01:00:51.180
They all dumped their stock!

01:00:51.520 --> 01:00:53.140
The company had to declare bankruptcy!

01:00:53.440 --> 01:00:53.640
What?

01:00:54.040 --> 01:00:55.000
This can't be true!

01:00:55.260 --> 01:00:56.660
Speed just won the company!

01:00:56.840 --> 01:00:58.960
Plus, we've got plans to make eco-friendly cars!

01:00:58.960 --> 01:00:59.980
The company is...

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:03.520
It's gone belly up! The only thing left is a six-pack of Ranford Cola!

01:01:03.740 --> 01:01:04.360
That's it?

01:01:04.560 --> 01:01:07.480
No. You also get 25,000 desks from their offices.

01:01:07.820 --> 01:01:10.560
Um, I think I'll pass on those. Give them to the school.

01:01:10.840 --> 01:01:12.660
And you get 25,000 chairs.

01:01:12.920 --> 01:01:14.240
Give those to the school, too.

01:01:14.400 --> 01:01:17.000
And you get 25,000 staplers.

01:01:17.120 --> 01:01:18.140
Just give them to the school.

01:01:18.520 --> 01:01:20.880
I can't believe it! We were going to be rich!

01:01:21.120 --> 01:01:24.680
And we were going to finally finish the Mach 6 and turn into an eco-car!

01:01:24.960 --> 01:01:26.820
I know. I am truly sorry.

01:01:27.140 --> 01:01:29.980
It's okay. Someday soon, we'll finish the gasless engine...

01:01:30.380 --> 01:01:30.780
the world.
